  "tagline": "Managed ClickHouse platform that turns SQL pipes into low-latency, versioned HTTP APIs.",
  "description": "Tinybird is a developer platform on top of managed ClickHouse: you ingest events over an HTTP Events API, Kafka or S3, write SQL 'pipes', and publish them as parameterized, authenticated REST endpoints. Projects are defined as code, versioned in Git, deployed via CLI, and can be run locally with the Tinybird Local container. It removes most ClickHouse operations and API plumbing, which makes it popular for user-facing analytics in SaaS products. You trade some control and portability for that convenience, and costs scale with processed data and requests.",
